# This Pim's secrets: copy to /etc/pim/secrets.env, `chmod 600` it (deploy.sh refuses it
# otherwise), and pass it to deploy.sh as --secrets. Never commit the copy. Uncomment only what
# you use; every one is optional. APP_CREDENTIALS_KEY and PIM_INGRESS_SECRET are not here: each
# has a file of its own (gen-app-credentials-key.sh, gen-ingress-secret.sh), so it is made, kept
# and backed up apart from these, and Caddy reads the ingress secret's without seeing the rest.
#
# Where a secret ends up: celld v0.6.3 keeps it, like every variable, in the deployment's
# manifest in the fleet bucket. See docs/celld.md, "Secrets".

# Sign-in besides passkeys (docs/reference.md, Deploy). Callback: https://<your Pim>/auth/oauth/<google|github|oidc>/callback
# PIM_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# PIM_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# PIM_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# PIM_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# PIM_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# PIM_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Apps that need an OAuth client of your own (docs/reference.md, the app list).
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_APP_ID=

# The OTLP collector's auth headers, if it takes any.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=
